==================================================
January 31 is the 31st day of the year in the  [LINK: (Gregorian calendar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_calendar] ;  334 days remain until the end of the year (335 in  [LINK: (leap years) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leap_year] ).


# EVENTS #

[LINK: (314) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/314]  –  [LINK: (Pope Sylvester I) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Sylvester_I]  is consecrated, as successor to the late  [LINK: (Pope Miltiades) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Miltiades] . [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-1]

[LINK: (1208) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1208]  – The  [LINK: (Battle of Lena) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Lena]  takes place between King  [LINK: (Sverker II of Sweden) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sverker_II_of_Sweden]  and his rival, Prince Eric, whose victory puts him on the throne as King  [LINK: (Eric X of Sweden) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_X_of_Sweden] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-2]

[LINK: (1266) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1266]  – The  [LINK: (Mudéjar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mud%C3%A9jar]  of Murcia, who had rebelled against the  [LINK: (Crown of Castile) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown_of_Castile]  during the  [LINK: (Mudéjar revolt of 1264–1266) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mud%C3%A9jar_revolt_of_1264%E2%80%931266] , surrender the city to  [LINK: (James I of Aragon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_I_of_Aragon]  after a  [LINK: (siege lasting a month) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conquest_of_Murcia_(1265%E2%80%931266)] . [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-3]

[LINK: (1504) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1504]  – The Treaty of Lyon ends the  [LINK: (Italian War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_War_of_1499%E2%80%931504] , confirming French domination of northern Italy, while Spain receives the  [LINK: (Kingdom of Naples) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Naples] .

[LINK: (1578) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578]  –  [LINK: (Eighty Years' War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eighty_Years%27_War]  and  [LINK: (Anglo-Spanish War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Spanish_War_(1585%E2%80%931604)] : The  [LINK: (Battle of Gembloux) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Gembloux_(1578)]  is a victory for Spanish forces led by  [LINK: (Don John of Austria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_John_of_Austria]  over a rebel army of  [LINK: (Dutch) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_people] ,  [LINK: (Flemish) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flemish_people] ,  [LINK: (English) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_people] ,  [LINK: (Scottish) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scottish_people] ,  [LINK: (German) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_language] ,  [LINK: (French) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_people]  and  [LINK: (Walloons) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walloons] . [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (1606) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1606]  –  [LINK: (Gunpowder Plot) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunpowder_Plot] : Four of the conspirators, including  [LINK: (Guy Fawkes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_Fawkes] , are executed for treason by  [LINK: (hanging, drawing and quartering) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanged,_drawn_and_quartered] , for plotting against  [LINK: (Parliament) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parliament_of_England]  and  [LINK: (King James) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_VI_and_I] . [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-5]

[LINK: (1609) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1609]  –   [LINK: (Wisselbank of Amsterdam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank_of_Amsterdam]  established [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-6]

[LINK: (1703) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1703]  –    [LINK: (Forty-seven rōnin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forty-seven_r%C5%8Dnin] , under the command of  [LINK: (Ōishi Kuranosuke) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%8Cishi_Yoshio] , avenged the death of their master, by killing  [LINK: (Kira Yoshinaka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kira_Yoshinaka] . [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-7]

[LINK: (1747) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1747]  – The first  [LINK: (venereal diseases) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venereal_disease]  clinic opens at  [LINK: (London Lock Hospital) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London_Lock_Hospital] .

[LINK: (1814) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1814]  –  [LINK: (Gervasio Antonio de Posadas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gervasio_Antonio_de_Posadas]  becomes  [LINK: (Supreme Director of the United Provinces of the Río de la Plata) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Director_of_the_United_Provinces_of_the_R%C3%ADo_de_la_Plata]  (present-day Argentina).

[LINK: (1846) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1846]  – After the  [LINK: (Milwaukee Bridge War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milwaukee_Bridge_War] , the United States towns of Juneautown and Kilbourntown unify to create the City of  [LINK: (Milwaukee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milwaukee] . [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-8]

[LINK: (1848) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1848]  –  [LINK: (John C. Frémont) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_C._Fr%C3%A9mont]  is  [LINK: (court-martialed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Court-martial]  for mutiny and disobeying orders.

[LINK: (1862) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1862]  –  [LINK: (Alvan Graham Clark) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alvan_Graham_Clark]  discovers the  [LINK: (white dwarf) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_dwarf]  star Sirius B, a companion of  [LINK: (Sirius) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirius] , through an 18.5-inch (47 cm) telescope now located at  [LINK: (Northwestern University) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northwestern_University] . [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-9]

[LINK: (1865) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1865]  –  [LINK: (American Civil War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War] : The  [LINK: (United States Congress) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Congress]  passes the  [LINK: (Thirteenth Amendment to the United States Constitution) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thirteenth_Amendment_to_the_United_States_Constitution] , abolishing slavery, and submits it to the states for ratification. [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-10]

1865   – American Civil War:  [LINK: (Confederate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confederate_States_of_America]  General  [LINK: (Robert E. Lee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_E._Lee]  becomes general-in-chief of all Confederate armies. [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-11]

[LINK: (1891) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1891]  –  [LINK: (History of Portugal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Portugal_(1834%E2%80%931910)] : The first attempt at a Portuguese  [LINK: (republican) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republicanism]  revolution breaks out in the northern city of  [LINK: (Porto) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porto] .

[LINK: (1900) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1900]  – Datu Muhammad Salleh is killed in Kampung Teboh, Tambunan, ending the  [LINK: (Mat Salleh Rebellion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mat_Salleh_Rebellion] .

[LINK: (1901) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1901]  –  [LINK: (Anton Chekhov) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anton_Chekhov] 's  [LINK: (Three Sisters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three_Sisters_(play)]  premieres at  [LINK: (Moscow Art Theatre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow_Art_Theatre]  in Russia. [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-12]

[LINK: (1915) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1915]  –  [LINK: (World War I) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_I] :  [LINK: (Germany) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_Empire]  is the first to make large-scale use of  [LINK: (poison gas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical_weapons_in_World_War_I]  in warfare in the  [LINK: (Battle of Bolimów) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Bolim%C3%B3w]  against  [LINK: (Russia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_Empire] . [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-13]

[LINK: (1917) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1917]  – World War I: Kaiser Wilhelm II orders the  [LINK: (resumption of unrestricted submarine warfare) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U-boat_Campaign#1917:_Resumption_of_unrestricted_submarine_warfare] .

[LINK: (1918) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1918]  – A  [LINK: (series of accidental collisions) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_May_Island]  on a misty Scottish night leads to the loss of two  [LINK: (Royal Navy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Navy]   [LINK: (submarines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Submarine]  with over a hundred lives, and damage to another five British warships.

1918   –  [LINK: (Finnish Civil War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_Civil_War] : The  [LINK: (Suinula massacre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_massacres_in_the_Finnish_Civil_War] , which changes the nature of the war in a more hostile direction, takes place in  [LINK: (Kangasala) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangasala] . [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-14]  [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-15]

[LINK: (1919) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1919]  – The  [LINK: (Battle of George Square) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_George_Square]  takes place in  [LINK: (Glasgow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glasgow] , Scotland, during a campaign for shorter working hours.

[LINK: (1928) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1928]  –  [LINK: (Leon Trotsky) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leon_Trotsky]  is exiled to  [LINK: (Alma-Ata) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alma-Ata] .

[LINK: (1942) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1942]  –  [LINK: (World War II) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II] : Allied forces are defeated by the Japanese at the  [LINK: (Battle of Malaya) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Malaya]  and retreat to Singapore.

[LINK: (1943) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1943]  – World War II: German field marshal  [LINK: (Friedrich Paulus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrich_Paulus]  surrenders to the Soviets at  [LINK: (Stalingrad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Stalingrad] , followed two days later by the remainder of his Sixth Army, ending one of the war's fiercest battles.

[LINK: (1944) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1944]  – World War II: American forces land on  [LINK: (Kwajalein Atoll) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kwajalein_Atoll]  and other islands in the Japanese-held  [LINK: (Marshall Islands) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshall_Islands] .

1944   – World War II: During the  [LINK: (Anzio campaign) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Anzio] , the  [LINK: (1st Ranger Battalion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1st_Ranger_Battalion]  (Darby's Rangers) is destroyed behind enemy lines in a heavily outnumbered encounter at  [LINK: (Battle of Cisterna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Cisterna] , Italy.

[LINK: (1945) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1945]  – US Army private  [LINK: (Eddie Slovik) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eddie_Slovik]  is  [LINK: (executed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_punishment]  for  [LINK: (desertion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desertion] , the first such execution of an American soldier since the  [LINK: (Civil War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War] .

1945   – World War II: About 3,000 inmates from the  [LINK: (Stutthof concentration camp) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stutthof_concentration_camp]  are forcibly marched into the  [LINK: (Baltic Sea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baltic_Sea]  at Palmnicken (now  [LINK: (Yantarny) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yantarny,_Kaliningrad_Oblast] , Russia) and executed.

1945   – World War II: The end of fighting in the  [LINK: (Battle of Hill 170) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Hill_170]  during the  [LINK: (Burma Campaign) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burma_Campaign] , in which the British  [LINK: (3 Commando Brigade) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3_Commando_Brigade]  repulsed a Japanese counterattack on their positions and precipitated a general retirement from the  [LINK: (Arakan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rakhine_State]  Peninsula.

[LINK: (1946) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1946]  –  [LINK: (Cold War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_War] :  [LINK: (Yugoslavia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socialist_Federal_Republic_of_Yugoslavia] 's new  [LINK: (constitution) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1946_Yugoslav_Constitution] , modeling that of the  [LINK: (Soviet Union) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_Union] , establishes six constituent republics ( [LINK: (Bosnia and Herzegovina) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socialist_Republic_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina] ,  [LINK: (Croatia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socialist_Republic_of_Croatia] ,  [LINK: (Macedonia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socialist_Republic_of_Macedonia] ,  [LINK: (Montenegro) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socialist_Republic_of_Montenegro] ,  [LINK: (Serbia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socialist_Republic_of_Serbia]  and  [LINK: (Slovenia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socialist_Republic_of_Slovenia] ).

