[LINK: (1968) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968]  –  [LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] :  [LINK: (Viet Cong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viet_Cong]  guerrillas attack the United States embassy in  [LINK: (Saigon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saigon] , and other attacks, in the early morning hours, later grouped together as the  [LINK: (Tet Offensive) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tet_Offensive] .

[LINK: (1971) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1971]  –  [LINK: (Apollo program) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_program] :  [LINK: (Apollo 14) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_14] : Astronauts  [LINK: (Alan Shepard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Shepard] ,  [LINK: (Stuart Roosa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_Roosa] , and  [LINK: (Edgar Mitchell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edgar_Mitchell] , aboard a  [LINK: (Saturn V) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturn_V] , lift off for a mission to the  [LINK: (Fra Mauro Highlands) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fra_Mauro_formation]  on the  [LINK: (Moon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon] .

1971   – The  [LINK: (Winter Soldier Investigation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_Soldier_Investigation] , organized by the  [LINK: (Vietnam Veterans Against the War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_Veterans_Against_the_War]  to publicize alleged  [LINK: (war crimes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_crime]  and atrocities by Americans and allies in  [LINK: (Vietnam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam] , begins in  [LINK: (Detroit) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detroit] .

[LINK: (1978) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1978]  – The  [LINK: (Crown of St. Stephen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Crown_of_Hungary]  (also known as the Holy Crown of Hungary) goes on public display after being returned to Hungary from the United States, where it was held after  [LINK: (World War II) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II] . [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-16]

[LINK: (1988) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1988]  –  [LINK: (Doug Williams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doug_Williams_(quarterback)]  becomes the first African American quarterback to play in a  [LINK: (Super Bowl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Bowl]  and leads the  [LINK: (Washington Redskins) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Redskins]  to victory in  [LINK: (Super Bowl XXII) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Bowl_XXII] . [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-17]

[LINK: (1996) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996]  – An explosives-filled truck rams into the gates of the  [LINK: (Central Bank of Sri Lanka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Bank_of_Sri_Lanka]  in  [LINK: (Colombo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colombo] , killing at least 86 people and injuring 1,400.

[LINK: (2000) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000]  –  [LINK: (Alaska Airlines Flight 261) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaska_Airlines_Flight_261]  crash: An  [LINK: (MD-83) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MD-83] , experiencing horizontal stabilizer problems, crashes in the Pacific Ocean off the coast of  [LINK: (Point Mugu, California) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_Mugu,_California] , killing all 88 aboard.

[LINK: (2001) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2001]  – In the Netherlands, a Scottish court convicts  [LINK: (Libyan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libya]   [LINK: (Abdelbaset al-Megrahi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abdelbaset_al-Megrahi]  and acquits another Libyan citizen for their part in the bombing of  [LINK: (Pan Am Flight 103) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pan_Am_Flight_103]  over  [LINK: (Lockerbie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lockerbie] , Scotland in 1988.

2001   – Two  [LINK: (Japan Airlines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Airlines]  planes  [LINK: (nearly collide) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2001_Japan_Airlines_mid-air_incident]  over  [LINK: (Suruga Bay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suruga_Bay]  in Japan. [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-Yomiuri-18]

[LINK: (2003) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2003]  – The  [LINK: (Waterfall rail accident) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waterfall_rail_accident]  occurs near  [LINK: (Waterfall, New South Wales) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waterfall,_New_South_Wales] , Australia. [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-Mcintosh-19]

[LINK: (2007) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007]  – Emergency officials in Boston mistakenly identify battery-powered LED placards depicting characters from  [LINK: (Aqua Teen Hunger Force) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_Teen_Hunger_Force]  as  [LINK: (Improvised explosive devices) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Improvised_explosive_device]  (IEDs), causing  [LINK: (a panic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_Boston_Mooninite_panic] . [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31#cite_note-20]

[LINK: (2009) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009]  – At least 113 people are killed in  [LINK: (Kenya) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenya]  and over 200 injured following an  [LINK: (oil spillage ignition) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Molo_fire]  in  [LINK: (Molo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Molo,_Kenya] , days after  [LINK: (a massive fire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009_Nakumatt_supermarket_fire]  at a  [LINK: (Nakumatt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nakumatt]  supermarket in  [LINK: (Nairobi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nairobi]  killed at least 25 people.

